[style name="our style"]
join renko left
renko: Great, where am I now? This place definitely isn’t the TORIFUNE anymore. And it’s super…creepy. I feel like I’m being watched. I swear I see eyes everywhere.
join merry left
merry: …
renko: Huh? Merry?! Is that you?!
merry: …
renko: Oh thank god, finally! Come on, let's get out of here!
merry: …
merry: Merry? What’s wrong?
unknown: She can’t hear you at the moment.
renko: ?!
unknown: Hello, Ms. Usami. Please let me promptly introduce myself.
join yukari left
yukari: I am Yukari Yakumo, or the mastermind behind this minor incident. And it's a pleasure to make your acquaintance.
renko: Well I'm not pleased! Why did you drag us here and what have you done to Merry?!
yukari: Fufufu. My, my you’re so upset. Ms. Hearn is just sleeping. As for yourself, why not just sit down for a few minutes? Rest your weary legs.
renko: No, no thank you.
renko: Do you have any idea what kind of hell I’ve been through? Between that creature that’s been chasing me and all those puzzles you made me do!
yukari: Ah yes, Nue did go a bit…overboard.
yukari: I assure you didn’t intend to have her be so aggressive. But what can you do? She’s such an ancient youkai and they are quite a handful.
yukari: An uncontrollable force of nature. Even more so when in an unknown environment.
renko: What a convenient explanation, but I don’t care! Give me back Merry now!
yukari: Ah, well you see no, I will not be doing that.
renko: What? Why?! I completed your tests, your trials, or whatever. So let her go!
yukari: Did you think going through all that was so that you could get her back?
renko: Huh?!
yukari: All these trials were a way to make sure you could survive the trip home, not for the both of you to go back.
renko: W-what do you mean by that?
yukari: Ms. Hearn’s powers are far too dangerous. It’s because of them the two of you were dragged here. Thus, it would be for the best if she stayed with me.
yukari: Don’t you think so too, Merry? It would be such a shame if you accidentally put your dear friend through such a tribulation again.
merry: …
renko: So…after all that you just want me to abandon her?
yukari: Think of it less like abandonment and more like…relinquishing her.
yukari: I’m sure she would feel oh so terrible if something this harrowing happened to you again. It would be horrible if she were saddened if something happened to you, correct?
renko: That’s, that’s true.
yukari: So you agree. It would be the safest for you to just…let her go.
renko: That’s also true…but…
yukari: But?
renko: But I don’t care! I don’t care what danger Merry might accidentally put me through.
renko: She’s my friend and I love her. So I don’t care what you are or what tests you make me to do! I’ll fight you as hard as I can to take her back!
yukari: …
renko: …?
yukari: Ohahahahaha!
yukari: Goodness, I’ve forgotten how entertaining humans can be. Brave and rather stupid too.
yukari: Well, it seems as if my warning has fallen of deaf ears, so very well you can have your Merry back.
renko: Really? Just like that? No tricks?
yukari: No, no tricks, but be warned a day will come where Maribel’s powers might spin out of control and when that time comes…
yukari: I will take her from you.
renko: Then if that happens, I’ll try my hardest to get her back, just like I did today.
merry: I will hold you to that, Renko.
leave yukari
renko: Damn…she’s creepy. I've got a bunch of goosebumps.
merry: Hmmm…ah?
renko: Merry, you’re awake! Are you alright?
merry: Yes, but I was having…such an odd dream.
merry: I saw you running around and this creature was chasing after you. And I also heard this woman’s voice. It was all so very confusing.
renko: Hehe, yeah that does sound like a weird dream. I’m just glad you’re okay. Can you move?
merry: I’m not in any pain so I think so, but oh my where are we? Is this where we ended up after going through that dark patch?
renko: Something like that. I still don’t see a way outta here though. I looked around why you were passed out, but couldn't find any clues.
merry: Hmm, well there’s something different about this space. Parts of it almost smell like Earth. I…I might be able to open a gap and get us back home.
renko: Really?!
merry: Hmhmm!
renko: Great!
renko: How about when we get back we go out for some coffee or tea? After all this, some time to unwind sounds great.
merry: Or maybe even some curry or omelets!
renko: Whatever works best for you Merry. I’ll follow you to the ends of the Earth.
renko: Or even deepest reaches of space.